# Database migrations

The initial Alembic revision is a frozen schema baseline. For a new database,
`python -m alembic upgrade head` creates the schema. Existing unversioned
databases are upgraded through the compatibility migration in
`database/init_db.py`, stamped at the baseline, and then advanced by Alembic.

Before upgrading an existing deployment, create and verify a database backup.
When changing models, generate a new revision with
`python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"`, inspect and
edit the generated operations, and run migration tests before release. Never
modify a revision that has already been applied to a deployment.

SQLite migrations run in batch mode. PostgreSQL migrations are represented by
the same SQLAlchemy/Alembic revisions but still require a live PostgreSQL
integration test before claiming the deployment path is verified.
